BT /F2 12 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg
50 514 Td (1. The Paradox of Modern Markets) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 498 Td (Digital markets have dramatically expanded the range of choices available to) Tj ET
50 485 Td (individual participants. Through platforms, search aggregators, and unbundled) Tj ET
50 472 Td (service feeds, buyers can explore an unprecedented array of suppliers, price) Tj ET
50 459 Td (points, and item configurations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 440 Td (Yet, this abundance of choice frequently coexists with a systemic contraction in) Tj ET
50 427 Td (collective market influence. While individuals possess extensive tools to navigate) Tj ET
50 414 Td (*within* the terms established by a marketplace, they possess diminishing) Tj ET
50 401 Td (structural capacity to shape those terms or contest the baseline assumptions of) Tj ET
50 388 Td (offer formation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 369 Td (This is the central tension of market isolation: **abundant individual choice) Tj ET
50 356 Td (paired with negligible collective voice**.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg
50 322 Td (2. Access Is Not Authority) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 306 Td (The foundational analytical distinction formulated in DC2SC Module 01 separates) Tj ET
50 293 Td (**access** from **authority**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 274 Td (  **Access \(Choice\):** The capacity to search among and select from an inventory) Tj ET
50 261 Td (of pre-configured offers under unilateral, take-it-or-leave-it terms.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 242 Td (  **Authority \(Voice\):** The institutional capacity to negotiate, influence, or) Tj ET
50 229 Td (ratify the terms, constraints, and baseline conditions of market exchange.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 210 Td (Digital platforms excel at optimizing access. They provide real-time filtering,) Tj ET
50 197 Td (algorithmic sorting, and low-friction checkout. However, this optimization is) Tj ET
50 184 Td (architecturally atomized: millions of individuals interact with the platform as) Tj ET
50 171 Td (millions of isolated sessions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
50 152 Td (Even when participants share identical household constraints, travel dates, or) Tj ET
50 139 Td (quality requirements, the market interface treats them as separate, price-taking) Tj ET
50 126 Td (price-elasticity points.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg
50 92 Td (3. The Limits of Individual Optimization) Tj ET
endstream
